-B is required for de novo centromere chromatin assembly on human alphoid DNA</article-title><source>J. Cell Biol.</source><year>2002</year><volume>159</volume><fpage>765</fpage><lpage>775</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12460987</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><label>8</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tomizuka</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Yoshida</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Uejima</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Kugoh</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Sato</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Ohguma</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Hayasaka</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hanaoka</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Oshimura</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Ishida</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Functional expression and germline transmission of a human chromosome fragment in chimaeric mice</article-title><source>Nat. Genet.</source><year>1997</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>133</fpage><lpage>143</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9171824</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Suzuki</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Nishii</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Okazaki</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Ikeno</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Human artificial chromosomes constructed using the bottom-up strategy are stably maintained in mitosis and efficiently transmissible to progeny mice</article-title><source>J. Biol. Chem.</source><year>2006</year><volume>281</volume><fpage>26615</fpage><lpage>26623</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16837455</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Henning</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name><name><surname>Novotny</surname><given-names>EA</given-names></name><name><surname>Compton</surname><given-names>ST</given-names></name><name><surname>Guan</surname><given-names>XY</given-names></name><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>PP</given-names></name><name><surname>Ashlock</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Human artificial chromosomes generated by modification of a yeast artificial chromosome containing both human alpha satellite and single-copy DNA sequences</article-title><source>Proc. Natl Acad. Sci. USA</source><year>1999</year><volume>96</volume><fpage>592</fpage><lpage>597</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9892678</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grimes</surname><given-names>BR</given-names></name><name><surname>Schindelhauer</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>McGill</surname><given-names>NI</given-names></name><name><surname>Ross</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ebersole</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name><name><surname>Cooke</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Stable gene expression from a mammalian artificial chromosome</article-title><source>EMBO Rep.</source><year>2001</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>910</fpage><lpage>914</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11571265</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mejia</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>